{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N7wMupDeNdxFKMBag4r3kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand the current state and determine what tasks to propose.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator).\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/<name>/` - One directory per utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing framework\n- `pkg/sys/` - System call abstractions\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `docs/specs/` - SRDs, use cases, test suites\n- `magefiles/` - Build automation\n\nLooking at the requirement_states and code_status, I can see which SRDs are marked as ready and which use cases haven't been started yet. In Release 00.0, the format utility and testutils framework are both flagged as not started, so those are the priority areas to focus on for the next implementation phase.\n\nScanning through the remaining releases, there's a significant backlog of unstarted use cases across multiple versions—cat, nproc, ls variants, logname, echo, tac, expand, cut, and several checksum utilities all need implementation work. This gives me a clear picture of what's pending across the roadmap. Looking at the requirement_states field to see which SRDs have all their requirements in ready status—I'm seeing a solid block of them from srd004 through srd085, with most showing complete readiness across the board. Continuing through the remaining utilities, I see srd108 through srd114 are all marked ready as well. But I need to step back and reconsider the constraint—I should only be proposing tasks for requirements with \"ready\" status, and I need to focus on the earliest incomplete release first. Let me examine the release states more carefully to see