{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N7wMupDeNdxFKMBag4r3kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The real goal is stress-testing the mage-claude-orchestrator AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). `cmd/<name>/` holds one package per utility. `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/`, `pkg/testutils/` provide shared infrastructure. SRDs in `docs/specs/` are the source of truth. Differential tests compare Go output against g-prefixed GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Implementation state**: Releases 00.0 through 08.0 are partially or fully implemented (many use cases show codestatus \"implemented\"). Several scattered utilities across releases remain \"not started\" (cat, nproc, logname, echo, tac, expand, cut, sha1sum, sha512sum, mktemp, groups, sort, mv, sleep, factor). The requirement_states field shows which SRDs currently have \"ready\" requirements awaiting generation.\n\n**Current release**: The earliest release with \"ready\" requirements in requirement_states is **08.1** (fmt, numfmt, od, printf). All four use cases have codestatus \"not started\" and all their requirements are \"ready\".\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 08.1 contains four SRDs with ready requirements:\n- srd070-fmt: 15 requirements (R2.1, R3.1, R4.1, R5.1, R6.1, R7.1, R8.1, R9.1, R10.1, R11.1, R12.1, R13.1-R13.4)\n- srd071-numfmt: 16 requirements\n- srd072-od: 16 requirements\n- srd073-printf: 16 requirements\n\nCanonical ordering (P8, alphabetical by file path): cmd/fmt first, then numfmt, od, printf. With a 4-task limit, I cover all 15 fmt requirements across 4 tasks.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\nAssuming default weight 1 for all srd070-fmt requirements (no weight-4 restructuring note for this SRD, unlike rel15.0):\n\n- Task 0: R2.1 (w=1) + R3.1 (w=1) + R4.1 (w=1) + R5.1 (w=1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 1: R6.1 (w=1) + R7.1 (w=1) + R8.1 (w=1) + R9.1 (w=1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 2: R10.1 (w=1) + R11.1 (w=1) + R12.1 (w=1) + R13.1 (w=1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 3: R13.2 (w=1) + R13.3 (w=1) + R13.4 (w=1) = 3 -- under limit\n\nAll tasks pass the weight-4 budget.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/fmt: srd070 R2.1-R5.1\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml (full SRD -- read all requirements, focus on R2.1, R3.1, R4.1, R5.1)\n      - pkg/sys/ (SIGPIPE handler via InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- DiffTest, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/fmt/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: fmt utility -- paragraph reformatting to specified width\n      - path: cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gfmt reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd070 R2.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd070 R3.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd070 R4.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd070 R5.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared SIGPIPE protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests with gfmt as reference binary from Homebrew coreutils\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in all differential test cases\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath for gfmt and t.Skip if not found per graceful skip protocol\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"Build binary with testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") from within cmd/fmt/ test\"\